wreckage is being recovered far and wide  as russian aviation officials try to  piece together what happened  some debris from the crash was found on  a mountainside in the far eastern region  of kamchatka  more pieces were fished out of the sea  other parts of the plane were found  about five kilometers from the airport's  runway  in the town of palana today a plane  following the route from petro pavlov's  kamchatsky to polana crashed  the tragedy is said to have occurred  during the landing presumably the plane  was making a second approach and  visibility was poor  air traffic control lost contact as the  plane neared its destination  heavy fog may have caused the plane to  go off course a criminal investigation  is underway  but the plane's owner says everything  was technically sound before takeoff  local officials have partially backed  this up confirming no problems were  detected with the russian-made antonov  aircraft before it departed  the aircraft was made in 1982 it has a  valid certificate of airworthiness  the crew passed a pre-flight inspection  currently  search and rescue activities are  underway all  28 people on board are believed dead but  so far  no bodies have been recovered a local  leader and two children were among the  passengers  the rugged terrain around polana is  making the search a slow and arduous  process  the area where the wreckage was found is  difficult to access  especially as night falls vinton monahan  al jazeera
 

